  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA of size NNN.\n\nYou can rearrange the elements of AAA as you want. After that, construct an array BBB of size NNN as:\n\n\nB1=A1B_1 = A_1B1​=A1​;\nBi=Bi−1B_i = B_{i - 1}Bi​=Bi−1​ &amp;\\&amp;&amp; AiA_iAi​ for all 2≤i≤N2 \\le i \\le N2≤i≤N, where &amp;\\&amp;&amp; denotes the bitwise AND operator.\nFind the **lexicographically largest** possible array BBB.\n\nFor two arrays XXX and YYY, both of size NNN, the array XXX is said to be lexicographically larger than array YYY, if, in the first position where XXX and YYY differ, Xi&gt;YiX_i \\gt Y_iXi​&gt;Yi​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains NNN, the size of the array AAA.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, NNN space separated integers denoting the lexicographically largest array BBB that can be formed by any rearrangement of AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1041 \\le T \\le 2 \\cdot 10^41≤T≤2⋅104",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1091 \\le A_i \\le 10^91≤Ai​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 2⋅1052 \\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
